From d34f7cfd31a9cebcaeb2377266b413ec3e444c85 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Michal=20Brng=C3=A1l?= <michal@brngal.sk>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 17:08:49 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 01/11] Fix CVE-2026-109618 and CVE-2026-109619 (backport to
 7.2.34)

Port of upstream php-src commit 712e60f9ed "Avoid state corruption via
bailout" (Arnaud Le Blanc, Ilija Tovilo), branch
PHP-7.4-CVE-2026-109618-109619, GHSA-w8hw-w9fx-j79w / GHSA-6wmf-4rv5-p3rp.

Differences from the 7.4 patch:
- shutdown_executor(): 7.2 keeps the fast-shutdown path in
  "if (fast_shutdown) {", so the handler/stack reset goes there; the
  EG(error_handling)/EG(exception) reset follows
  zend_objects_store_free_object_storage().
- array_init_singleton()/zend_new_array_singleton(): 7.2 has no
  zend_new_array(); built on _zend_hash_init() with nTableSize = 1.
- ZSTR_MAX_OVERHEAD/ZSTR_MAX_LEN backported from 7.3 (zend_string.h).
- ZEND_CONCAT/ZEND_FAST_CONCAT: 7.2 had no overflow check at all; the
  check is added to both branches of both handlers in zend_vm_def.h and
  to the same 18 specialisations in zend_vm_execute.h (same text the
  generator would emit; re-run Zend/zend_vm_gen.php to double-check).
- HT_HASH_RESET: 7.2 has no SSE2 variant, nothing to change.
- max_multipart_body_parts (new INI, default -1 = max_input_vars +
  max_file_uploads) comes with the rfc1867 part, as in the 7.4 patch.
- session: "|| 1" instead of "|| true".

Behaviour change: memory_limit exhaustion and allocation overflows no
longer raise a catchable fatal error; the process prints the fatal error
to stderr and _exit(1)s. Session upload progress is disabled
unconditionally.

Not compiled or tested yet.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
