From 8db97ca755521b0c7e5cc3ef1ace1ecdb3034a15 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Michal=20Brng=C3=A1l?= <michal@brngal.sk>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 16:44:07 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 03/11] Fix GHSA-qc49-hpvq-g2w6 (CVE-2026-129289): drain unread
 request bodies

Opening php://input could create a request body stream without
consuming the input from the SAPI, and sapi_deactivate() took the
stream as proof the body had been read, so the drain was skipped.
Unread FastCGI STDIN bytes could then be parsed as a new request on a
FCGI_KEEP_CONN connection (request smuggling).

Backport of php-src c7a30157f6 to 7.2.34:
- main/SAPI.c: drain whenever post_read is false, independently of
  whether the request body stream exists (in 7.2 the code lives in
  sapi_deactivate(), not sapi_deactivate_module()).
- main/fastcgi.c: refuse a new FastCGI request if the previous STDIN
  record was only partially consumed; reset in_len in fcgi_close().
- Tests unread-body-keep-conn.phpt and unread-body-partial-record.phpt
  adapted to PHP 7.2 syntax (closure instead of arrow fn, strpos()
  instead of str_contains()).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
